      "text": "To find the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 3 and 6, we need to find the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 6.\n\nTo find the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 6, we can use the greatest common factor (GCF) of 6 and 1000 (the range of three-digit numbers).\n\nGCF(6, 1000) = 2\n\nTherefore, to find the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 6, we can simply divide 999 by 2 and add 3 (the remainder of the division) to the result.\n\n999 / 2 = 499\n\nTherefore, the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 6 is 999 + 3 = 1002.\n\nThe answer is 1002.",
